  "prefLabel": "Jus 2001.09 “Deputy chief medical examiner” (DCME) means the licensed physician certified by the American Board of Pathology as a qualified pathologist and appointed pursua",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Jus 2001.09 “Deputy chief medical examiner” (DCME) means the licensed physician certified by the American Board of Pathology as a qualified pathologist and appointed pursuant to RSA 611-A:1-a, to investigate deaths under the professional direction and supervision of the chief medical examiner and acts as the chief medical examiner whenever the latter is absent, or unable to act from any cause.\n\nSource. #8937, eff 7-14-07",
